  "validation_behavior": [
    "Clear the existing BYTE gate at43A594 before readiness or any query. A failure ordinarily leaves it0 regardless of its old fullBYTE value.",
    "Require actual readiness, successful number-of-tracks MCI query and one unsigned scan yielding2. Query exactly tracks1 and2.",
    "For each track, set TMSF format and require success; build type query with sprintf. MCI receives the same256-byte stack buffer as command and response; this alias is preserved.",
    "Track1 must not compare equal to audio under the modeled ASCII case-insensitive CRT boundary; no exact data text comparison or track1 length query occurs. Track2 must compare equal to audio.",
    "For track2, successful length query and three unsigned scanned fields are required; only first field is compared with34. Seconds and frames are parsed but unchecked. One escaped unsigned local is reused for count, audio predicate and parsed minutes; ordinary expected-minute array0,34 produces the original frame without steering.",
    "Set gateBYTE1 only after every check. Arbitrary response domains, general CRT locale and actual CD hardware behavior remain outside finite proof."
  ],
  "caller_behavior": [
    "Reset the existing sixDWORD MCI cells in observed order, including opened, before first readiness call.",
    "Capture readiness return, then always run actual validation. Exit successfully only if the saved readiness is nonzero and the live fullBYTE gate is nonzero. Validation success cannot replace a previously false readiness return.",
    "Otherwise call MessageBoxA with current owner, original text/title and0x35 flags. Exactly result2 cancels; every other tested result retries. Cancel does not clear the current gate, so a successful validator or modeled dialog callback mutation can leave a nonzero gate.",
    "Re-read window owner at the message boundary. Retrying repeats readiness/validation without resetting the six cells again."
  ],
